# File: tests/features/add_greeting_uppercase_count_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/221-add-greeting-uppercase-count-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Count ASCII uppercase letters in the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Count ASCII uppercase letters in the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_uppercase_count is called with Ada and with ABC XYZ
    Then the results are the Python int values 2 and 7

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Count only the 26 ASCII capitals
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_uppercase_count is called with bob 42!, Émile spelled with precomposed U+00C9, and fullwidth U+FF22 U+FF23
    Then the results are 1, 1, and 1

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_uppercase_count is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_uppercase_count of Ada
    Then it prints 2 and greeting_uppercase_count is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the ASCII A-Z set, completed-greeting scope, and inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0
